// The sheet's own variant is SelfBuff, but its range (9m) and aoe ("multi-target") describe a
// ranged group buff, not an effect that can land only on the caster
// (common/src/states/self_buff.rs: SelfBuff always targets the caster). This deviates to
// BasicAura -- the same multi-target ally-touch shape already used for water_breathing.ron in
// this folder, whose sheet entry has near-identical range/aoe/notes -- rather than the literal
// SelfBuff label, which cannot structurally deliver a multi-target effect.
//
// "Steps firm against water, mud, snow, or molten flows as though walking on solid earth" maps
// directly onto the existing FreedomOfMovement buff (immunity to DifficultTerrain, which is what
// models exactly this kind of surface-based movement penalty elsewhere in this folder) -- a
// strong fit, not a stretch substitution. The still-burned-by-lava carve-out has no separate
// hook and is dropped.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: FreedomOfMovement,
            strength: 1.0,
            duration: Some(3600.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(1.0),
    range: 9.0,
    energy_cost: 55.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Transmutation), source: Some(Primordial), cooldown: Some(20.0)),
)
